8. Emulating a post-test loop
Python does not have a built-in post-test loop. However, we can emulate one.
A post-test structure is useful when the loop body must execute at least once before the termination condition is checked.
One possible form is:
while True:

    n = int(
        input(
            "Enter a whole number between 1 and 100: "
        )
    )

    if n &gt;= 1 and n &lt;= 100:
        print("Thank you")
        break
Another solution uses a logical variable:
more = True

while more:

    n = int(
        input(
            "Enter a whole number between 1 and 100: "
        )
    )

    if n &gt;= 1 and n &lt;= 100:
        more = False
        print("Thank you")
The second form avoids break and makes the loop condition explicit.

